  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "As reported by Richard Green on the dev mailing list, the web admin fails with an error when attempting to include encoded characters, using name encoding, within XML datastream content. Using number encoding for these characters works fine. See a list of name and number encodings here: ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.ascii.cl/htmlcodes.htm"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.ascii.cl/htmlcodes.htm",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ".",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "As an example, adding the line <dc:rights>&#169; Fedora Commons</dc:rights> to a DC datastream works fine, but attempting to add <dc:rights>&copy; Fedora Commons</dc:rights> fails with the error \"The entity 'copy' was referenced but not declared\". A few name encoded characters do work (such as &lt; and &gt",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "id": "1f609",
        "shortName": ":wink:",
        "text": "😉"
       },
       "type": "emoji"
      },
      {
       "text": " but most do not.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The same errors are thrown when attempting this through the swing admin.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A note from Peter Cliff on this issue: ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "You need to define entities with names (&copy",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "id": "1f609",
        "shortName": ":wink:",
        "text": "😉"
       },
       "type": "emoji"
      },
      {
       "text": " etc.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "See:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.xml.com/pub/a/98/08/xmlqna2.html"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.xml.com/pub/a/98/08/xmlqna2.html",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.tizag.com/xmlTutorial/xmlentity.php"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.tizag.com/xmlTutorial/xmlentity.php",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So my guess is that somewhere some XML parsing/creating is happening",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "behind the scenes of that client and it is throwing the whole thing off",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "when the XML processing fails on account of an undefined entity?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I couldn't find any entity definitions for the HTML named ones in the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "src/xsd/ (aside from the reference in xhtml1-strict.xsd). Do there need",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "to be some?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
